      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:19:6",
      "text": [
        " رَأَيْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) قَدْ أُتِيَ بِقَدَحٍ مِنْ مَاءٍ فِيهِ ضَبَّةٌ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ فَرَأَيْتُهُ يَنْزِعُهَا بِأَسْنَانِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Salih Bin Al Sandy, from Ja’far Bin Basheer, from Amro Bin Abu Al Miqdam who said, ",
          "‘I saw Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having been brought a cup of water in which was a handle of silver, so I saw him<sup>asws</sup> remove it by his<sup>asws</sup> teeth’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from Salih ibn al-Sindiy from Ja‘far ibn Bashir from ‘ Arnr ibn abu Miqdam who has said the following: “I saw abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, when a bowl of water was brought to him (the Imam) in which there was a patch of silver, removing it with his teeth.’” "
        ]
      }
